---
layout: layout.jinja
title: Contact us
description: Questions about a snack, a subscription or a sighting? Write to Squatch Snacks.
permalink: /contact/
---
{#- A Netlify form: Netlify finds it in the built HTML (data-netlify), keeps what's sent, and shows /thanks/ after. bot-field is the honeypot. -#}
<Section id="write" level="1" title="Write to the ranger station" intro="Questions about a snack, a subscription, wholesale, or something you saw on the trail. We answer within two working days.">
	<form name="contact" method="POST" action="/thanks/" data-netlify="true" netlify-honeypot="bot-field" class="form">
		<input type="hidden" name="form-name" value="contact">
		<p hidden><label>Leave this empty: <input type="text" name="bot-field" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off"></label></p>
		<p>
			<label for="contact-name">Your name</label>
			<input id="contact-name" type="text" name="name" required autocomplete="name">
		</p>
		<p>
			<label for="contact-email">Email</label>
			<input id="contact-email" type="email" name="email" required autocomplete="email">
		</p>
		<p>
			<label for="contact-topic">What's it about?</label>
			<select id="contact-topic" name="topic">
				{%- for topic in ["A snack", "A subscription", "Wholesale", "A sighting", "Something else"] %}
				<option>{{ topic }}</option>
				{%- endfor %}
			</select>
		</p>
		<p>
			<label for="contact-message">Message</label>
			<textarea id="contact-message" name="message" rows="6" required></textarea>
		</p>
		<p><button type="submit" class="button">Send it</button></p>
	</form>
	<p class="muted">Or email <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>.</p>
</Section>
